# Example contents for the optional PREVIEW_ENV repository secret.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line (no `export`, no multi-line values).
# Store the whole block as ONE repo (or environment) secret named PREVIEW_ENV.
#
# These values are available to compose for ${KEY} interpolation, and to any
# service that sets `env_file: [${PREVIEW_ENV_FILE}]`.
#
# Use throwaway / preview-only credentials. Anyone who can push a branch to this
# repo can read them (their code runs in the preview), so never put production
# secrets here.

ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-me-with-a-preview-only-key
# THIRD_PARTY_API_KEY=...
